### IPP-1008 Backup reminder ("Last full backup: X days ago") tests
### Put the admin password while testing, then put CHANGE_ME back.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000/api
@adminEmail = askedin143@gmail.com
@adminPassword = CHANGE_ME
@adminToken = {{adminLogin.response.body.data.token}}


### 1. Admin login -> expect 200
# @name adminLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{adminEmail}}", "password": "{{adminPassword}}" }


### 2. Last backup -> expect 200, data.lastBackup = null (never) or { at, by, users, questions, quizAttempts, changesSince }
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/backup/last
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### 3. Content-only export -> expect data.lastBackup missing (content only does NOT count as a backup)
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/backup/export?scope=content
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### 4. Full export -> expect data.lastBackup { at: now, by: admin email, users: N, ... }
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/backup/export
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### 5. Last backup again -> expect at = time of request 4, changesSince all 0
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/backup/last
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### 6. Stats -> expect data.lastBackup (same as 5); the admin dashboard shows a green box "Last full backup: today"
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/stats
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### 7. By hand: Admin -> Users -> give a test user full access -> dashboard box turns amber:
###    "Not in that backup yet: 1 new paid user, 1 user new or changed" + "Download backup now".
###    Download a full backup -> green again. Older than 7 days -> amber.


### 8. Not logged in -> expect 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/backup/last
